From 6404fc5bef4b8869ed669d954d822c94370ec7df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 07:55:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00987/11171] [outer-loop] Flag exp3959 M3-efficiency 24.7x:
 verifier NOT in loop + simulated, not a real measurement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The .366 'M3 efficiency on REAL games — the load-bearing verifier-earns-its-place datum'
claimed efficiency_ratio=24.662x (cis_non_overlapping_pruner_helps). Adversarial review:

1. VERIFIER NOT IN LOOP: with-arm p=1/num_objects (object selection), without-arm
   p=target_area/total_pixels (random-pixel). The energy-verifier/induced model is never
   invoked; 24.7x is just object-vs-pixel search geometry.
2. SIMULATED, NOT MEASURED: both arms are simulate_geometric() draws from those assumed
   probabilities, NOT the agent run with vs without the verifier on the live env counting
   real actions — despite inference_substrate claiming 'real games'.
3. SURPRISING + UNREPLICATED: 24.7x vs the prior honest 1.96x (exp3929, a flagged
   tautology) and ~4x peer.

Stamped flagged_adversarial + corrigendum_2026_06_09 so the capstone (which skips
flagged artifacts) won't headline 24.7x. The REAL M3 proof — same agent WITH the
energy-verifier pruner vs WITHOUT on the actual env, counting real actions-to-solve —
remains UNMET. The two ARC solves (r11l/lp85 L1) are real + independently verified; this
flag is only about the misattributed efficiency number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
